  BUG: find_peaks() fails if x.flags.writable = False
### Describe your issue.

If the writable flag has been set to False on a np.array, then find_peaks() fails with a ValueError: buffer source array is read-only.
 
It seems that the View.MemoryView functions require writable arrays, but then why are they called "View"?


### Reproducing Code Example

```python
import numpy, scipy.signal

x = numpy.linspace(0,1,100)
x.flags.writeable = False
p = scipy.signal.find_peaks(x)
```


